# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/capital_heists.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event job_way_out
# en: Gone by Morning
title [d8c8b3] = 天亮前脱身
# en: {job_loot == 0: You get away with nothing but your skin, and a heart going like a drum.|{job_loot <= 2: You get away with a few things under your coat, each worth more than it looks.|{job_loot <= 4: You get away with a real bundle: {job_where == 2: silver, a necklace, letters on thick paper|tea, silk, something in bottles that clinks when you walk}.|You get away with more than your coat will hold, and walk very carefully.}}} {job_where == 2: Behind you the Crescent's windows are going dark one by one, and the last carriages are leaving.|Behind you the customs lamp burns on over the wharf, and the gulls are waking.}
text [0ec807] = {job_loot == 0: 你脱了身，除了一身皮肉和一颗咚咚直跳的心，什么也没带出来。|{job_loot <= 2: 你脱了身，外套底下藏着几样东西，每样都比看上去值钱。|{job_loot <= 4: 你脱了身，带着一大包：{job_where == 2: 银器、一条项链、几封厚纸写的信|茶叶、丝绸，还有走起来叮当响的瓶装货}。|你脱了身，带的东西多得外套都装不下，走得小心翼翼。}}} {job_where == 2: 身后，新月街的窗户一扇接一扇暗下去，最后几辆马车正在离开。|身后，海关的灯还在码头上亮着，海鸥正在醒来。}
# en: A student slipping along a dark harbour-town lane at the grey end of night, a heavy bundle under one arm, the arches of a great bridge ahead.
scene [f09788] = 天将破晓时，一个学生沿着港城一条黑暗的小巷溜走，胳膊下夹着一个沉甸甸的包，前方是一座大桥的桥拱。
# en: {job_loot == 0: Go to bed as the gulls wake|Fence it under the bridge}
opt.left.label [0d1195] = {job_loot == 0: 趁海鸥醒来时上床|到桥底下销赃}
# en: {job_loot == 0: Sleep, for what's left of the night.|Crowns, by what you carry. A little Hollow.}
opt.left.hint [fb08af] = {job_loot == 0: 趁夜里还剩一点，睡一觉。|克朗，看你带出来多少。会偏向空洞一点。}
# en: {job_loot == 0: There's nothing to fence. You go to bed as the gulls wake up, and sleep like a stone till noon.|{&{flag(undercroft_known): The fence in the velvet waistcoat, in his alcove off the Undercroft's dice hall, weighs it through his loupe and pays, politely, while the river drips through the roof.|Somebody's cousin takes you down to the old cellars under the middle bridge, where a fence in a velvet waistcoat weighs it through his loupe and pays, politely.}|A fence under the middle bridge takes it all without looking and pays without counting, which means she counted before you came.|The fence pays, pours you a drink, and asks where you'll be working next. You don't tell her.}}
opt.left.say.1 [41cb19] = {job_loot == 0: 没东西可销。你在海鸥醒来时上床，一觉睡到中午，睡得像块石头。|{&{flag(undercroft_known): 那个穿天鹅绒背心的销赃人坐在地下赌窟赌厅旁的凹室里，透过放大镜掂量了一番，客客气气地付了钱，河水从顶上滴下来。|有人的表亲领你下到中桥底下的老地窖，一个穿天鹅绒背心的销赃人透过放大镜掂量了一番，客客气气地付了钱。}|中桥底下的一个销赃女人看也不看就全收了，付钱也不数，这说明她在你来之前就数过了。|销赃人付了钱，给你倒了杯酒，问你下一回在哪儿干活。你没告诉她。}}
# en: {job_loot == 0: Tell the story down the lanes|Give it away down the lanes}
opt.right.label [c163ee] = {job_loot == 0: 沿着小巷讲这个故事|沿着小巷分给人家}
# en: {job_loot == 0: A good story, where it will travel. No sleep.|Renown in Port Calder, by what you carry. No crowns.}
opt.right.hint [64c21e] = {job_loot == 0: 一个好故事，讲在传得开的地方。没得睡。|在考尔德港的名声，看你带出来多少。没有克朗。}
# en: {job_loot == 0: There's nothing to give away but a good story, so you sit up on the washhouse steps till breakfast and give that away instead. By noon half of Port Calder has heard it, and improved it.|{&Before dawn you leave it on doorsteps along Ashby Lane and the streets round it: {job_where == 2: a silver spoon or a ring on every step|tea, silk, a bottle on every step}. By noon all Port Calder is telling the story, and nobody tells the watch. Your purse is as light as it was.|You pawn what won't go through a letterbox and push the coins through the ones that will. Not a crown of it is yours by breakfast.|You give it to the women at the washhouse to share out, and they do, fairly, and better than you would. You keep nothing.}}
opt.right.say.1 [f67fbf] = {job_loot == 0: 没东西可分，只有一个好故事，于是你在洗衣房的台阶上坐到早饭，把这个故事分了出去。到中午，半个考尔德港都听说了，还添油加醋了一番。|{&天亮前你把东西放在阿什比巷和附近几条街的门阶上：{job_where == 2: 每级台阶上一把银勺或一枚戒指|茶叶、丝绸，每级台阶一瓶}。到了中午，整个考尔德港都在讲这件事，却没人去告诉巡夜队。你的钱袋还是一样轻。|塞不进信箱的你拿去当了，把硬币从塞得进的信箱口塞进去。到早饭时，一个克朗也不是你的了。|你把东西交给洗衣房的女人们去分，她们分得很公道，比你分得好。你什么也没留。}}

@event job_slip
# en: Flat in the Shadows
title [78e93b] = 贴在阴影里
# en: {job_where == 2: A footman with a candle comes round the turn of the back stair, and you go backwards through the nearest door into a cloakroom full of furs, cracking your hip on a coat-stand on the way. {job_dropped == 1: Something from your pockets is lying on the stair carpet outside, in plain view.|} The candle stops outside the door. He's young, and nervous, and he's heard something.|The watchman's dog finds your trail before the watchman does. You go up and over a stack of tea chests and skin your knuckles on the iron hoops{job_dropped == 1:, and something you were carrying drops into the black gap between the chests and stays there|}. Below you, the watchman calls the dog, and the dog doesn't come.} {job_cover > 0: You've one more near thing in you, maybe.|That was your last near thing.}
text [9c541c] = {job_where == 2: 一个端着蜡烛的男仆从后楼梯的拐角转过来，你倒退着钻进最近的一扇门，进了一间挂满毛皮大衣的衣帽间，路上胯骨撞在了衣帽架上。{job_dropped == 1: 你口袋里掉出来的一样东西就躺在外面楼梯的地毯上，明晃晃的。|}蜡烛在门外停下了。他年纪轻，有点紧张，他听见了什么。|守夜人的狗比守夜人先找到了你的踪迹。你爬上一摞茶叶箱翻过去，指节在铁箍上蹭破了皮{job_dropped == 1:，你带的一样东西掉进了箱子之间的黑缝里，再也够不着|}。下面，守夜人在唤狗，狗却不过去。} {job_cover > 0: 你大概还能再险一次。|那是你最后一次有惊无险。}
# en: A student pressed into a dark hiding place at night, nursing a scraped hand, as a light passes just outside.
scene [e34f48] = 夜里，一个学生紧贴在一处黑暗的藏身地，捂着擦破的手，一道光正从外面经过。
# en: {job_where == 2: Wait in the furs, then go|Over the back wall, and away}
opt.left.label [93a13d] = {job_where == 2: 在毛皮堆里等着，再走|翻过后墙，走人}
# en: {job_where == 2: You wait among the furs until the candle goes back down the stair, then let yourself out by the servants' door into the mews, limping a little.|You go over the back wall onto the wharf with your knuckles bleeding, and leave the dog barking at the place where you were.}
opt.left.say.1 [f9f56c] = {job_where == 2: 你在毛皮大衣中间等着，直到蜡烛顺着楼梯下去，才从仆人门溜进马厩巷，走路有点瘸。|你翻过后墙落到码头上，指节还在流血，留下那条狗冲着你刚才待过的地方狂叫。}
# en: {job_where == 2: Lie to him, and go on|Wait under the chests, then on}
opt.right.label [eeacdb] = {job_where == 2: 骗过他，继续往前|躲在箱子底下，再往前}
# en: {job_where == 2: On, by a lie: the next slip may not be a near thing.|On: the next slip may not be a near thing.}
opt.right.hint [fe7500] = {job_where == 2: 靠一句谎话往前：下一次失手未必还能有惊无险。|往前：下一次失手未必还能有惊无险。}
# en: {job_where == 2: You step out with your best guest's smile and ask him, a little drunkenly, where the cloakroom is. He shows you, very politely, and you're back in the house before he thinks to wonder which cloakroom you had been in.|You lie in the dark between the chests, smelling tea and your own skinned knuckles, until the watchman drags the dog off to finish his round. Then you go on.}
opt.right.say.1 [9252b2] = {job_where == 2: 你挂上最体面的客人笑容走出去，带着点醉意问他衣帽间在哪儿。他非常客气地给你指了路，等他想起来琢磨你刚才是在哪间衣帽间里，你早已回到宅子里了。|你躺在箱子之间的黑暗里，闻着茶叶和自己蹭破的指节的味道，直到守夜人把狗拖走去巡完他那一圈。然后你继续往前。}

@event job_caught
# en: The Watch
title [25c367] = 巡夜队
# en: A lantern comes up full in your face, and a second one behind it: {job_where == 2: the footmen have sent for the city watch|the city watch}. {job_loot == 0: {job_where == 2: You're somewhere in the house on the Crescent that no guest has any reason to be, and empty pockets convince nobody.|You're inside the customs' wall at night, empty-handed, which convinces nobody.}|You're {job_where == 2: in a house on the Crescent with your pockets full of somebody else's things|inside the customs' wall at night with your arms full of the crown's goods}, and the sergeant holds out his hand for every last thing.} {job_warned == 1: The sergeant knows your face, and says so.|The sergeant looks you over, scarf and wand and all, and sighs.}
text [a0aab8] = 一盏灯笼迎面照得你睁不开眼，后面还有第二盏：{job_where == 2: 男仆们叫来了城里的巡夜队|城里的巡夜队}。{job_loot == 0: {job_where == 2: 你待在新月街宅子里一个客人根本没理由去的地方，空口袋说服不了任何人。|你深夜在海关的墙里，两手空空，这说服不了任何人。}|你{job_where == 2: 在新月街的宅子里，口袋里塞满了别人的东西|深夜在海关的墙里，怀里抱满了王室的货}，巡长伸出手，要你一样不落地交出来。} {job_warned == 1: 巡长认得你这张脸，还说了出来。|巡长把你从头打量到脚，围巾、魔杖，一样没落，叹了口气。}
# en: Two city watchmen with lanterns and staves cornering a student at night, a sergeant with a notebook behind them.
scene [e42a9b] = 夜里两个提着灯笼、拿着棍子的城市巡夜人把一个学生堵住，后面一个拿着本子的巡长。
# en: Go quietly
opt.left.label [250d1c] = 老老实实跟他们走
# en: {job_warned == 1: {flag(job_booked): A night in the cells again, and in the morning the same magistrate, who remembers you and doubles the fine.|A night in the cells, and in the morning a magistrate with the sergeant's note about your face in front of him, who doubles the fine.} Your purse won't be the same this break.|A night in the cells with a drunk who sings, and in the morning a magistrate who fines you a sum that makes your eyes water and tells you to go back to your castle.}
opt.left.say.1 [849218] = {job_warned == 1: {flag(job_booked): 又是一夜牢房，早上又是同一个治安官，他记得你，罚金翻倍。|一夜牢房，早上的治安官面前摆着巡长记下你这张脸的字条，罚金翻倍。}这个假期你的钱袋是缓不过来了。|一夜牢房，同屋是个唱歌的醉汉，早上一个治安官罚了你一笔让你眼睛发酸的钱，叫你回你的城堡去。}
# en: Run for it
opt.right.label [38d292] = 拔腿就跑
# en: {job_loot == 0: You run, and {job_where == 2: the dark of the Royal Gardens hides you|Port Calder's lanes hide you the way they hide everyone}. You also know the sergeant saw your face.|You drop the lot at the sergeant's feet and run, and {job_where == 2: the dark of the Royal Gardens hides you|Port Calder's lanes hide you the way they hide everyone}. You also know the sergeant saw your face.}
opt.right.say.1 [4da75e] = {job_loot == 0: 你跑了，{job_where == 2: 皇家花园的黑暗藏住了你|考尔德港的小巷像藏所有人一样藏住了你}。你也知道巡长看清了你的脸。|你把所有东西扔在巡长脚边就跑，{job_where == 2: 皇家花园的黑暗藏住了你|考尔德港的小巷像藏所有人一样藏住了你}。你也知道巡长看清了你的脸。}
# en: {job_warned == 1: You run a street and into a third watchman. A night in the cells, a bruised jaw, and a magistrate who {flag(job_booked): remembers you|has the sergeant's note about your face} and doubles the fine.|You run a street and into a third watchman. A night in the cells, a bruised jaw, and in the morning a fine that empties your purse.}
opt.right.say.2 [a8e74b] = {job_warned == 1: 你跑了一条街，撞上了第三个巡夜人。一夜牢房，一块青肿的下巴，还有一个{flag(job_booked): 记得你|手上有巡长记下你这张脸的字条}的治安官，罚金翻倍。|你跑了一条街，撞上了第三个巡夜人。一夜牢房，一块青肿的下巴，早上一笔掏空你钱袋的罚金。}

@event docks_bonded_talk
# en: The Richest Floor
title [414180] = 全城最富的地板
# en: An old man on a wharf bench, one leg and a crutch, sees you looking at the long wall with the broken glass on top. "The bonded warehouses," he says. "Everything that comes into Port Calder waits in there till its duty's paid. Richest floor in the city. Forty years I walked it with a lantern." He spits. "Pensioned me off with nothing. Dogs, a round every hour, and a strongroom you could live in."
text [890812] = 码头长凳上一个独腿拄拐的老人，看见你在望那堵墙头插着碎玻璃的长墙。“保税仓库，”他说，“进考尔德港的东西，交清关税之前都在里面等着。全城最富的一层地板。我提着灯在那上面走了四十年。”他啐了一口。“打发我走，什么也没给。狗，每个钟头巡一圈，还有个大得能住人的保险库。”
# en: An old one-legged ex-watchman on a bench on a wharf at dusk, pointing with his crutch at a long walled warehouse with broken glass along its top, a student sitting beside him.
scene [2e6ee3] = 黄昏时码头长凳上一个独腿的退休看守，用拐杖指着一座墙头插着碎玻璃的长围墙仓库，一个学生坐在他身边。
# en: Buy him supper for the rest
opt.left.label [c27bfe] = 请他吃顿晚饭，听他说完
# en: You buy him a pie and a pint, and he tells you all of it: the dogs' names, the hour the round turns, the strongroom's iron door with the crown on it. "Not that you'd do anything," he says, and winks.
opt.left.say.1 [72c69f] = 你请他吃了个馅饼喝了一品脱，他全告诉了你：狗的名字，巡夜转弯的钟点，那扇铸着王冠的保险库铁门。“当然啦，你也不会干什么，”他说着，眨了眨眼。
# en: Tell him you're not that sort
opt.right.label [0fee9f] = 告诉他你不是那种人
# en: "Course you're not," he says. "Nobody is." He tells you anyway, the dogs' names and the round and the iron door, to the gulls, loud enough for you to hear. Walking away you find you've remembered every word, and feel grubby for it.
opt.right.say.1 [2abda5] = “当然不是，”他说，“谁都不是。”他还是讲了，狗的名字、巡夜、那扇铁门，对着海鸥讲，声音大得刚好让你听见。走开时你发现自己一个字都记住了，心里觉得有点脏。

@event bonded_customs_lamp
# en: The Customs Lamp
title [78100e] = 海关的灯
# en: {seen(bonded_customs_lamp) > 1: The wharf at night, the wall, the lamp, the dogs barking once at a cat and settling. The man who keeps the yard dogs comes out of a side gate for his pipe. The lantern goes round.|From the shadow of a crane on the wharf you can see the whole of it: the long wall with glass along the top, the customs house with one lamp burning, and inside the yard a watchman's lantern going round like the hand of a slow clock. A man comes out of a side gate with the yard dogs' leashes over his arm, for his pipe.}
text [60d41f] = {seen(bonded_customs_lamp) > 1: 夜里的码头，墙，灯，狗冲一只猫叫了一声又安静下来。管看门狗的人从侧门出来抽烟斗。灯笼一圈圈地转。|从码头一架吊车的阴影里，你能看清全貌：墙头插着玻璃的长墙，海关房子里亮着一盏灯，院子里看守的灯笼一圈圈地转，像一只慢钟的指针。一个男人胳膊上搭着看门狗的皮带从侧门出来，抽烟斗。}
# en: Night on a harbour wharf, a long warehouse wall topped with broken glass, a single lamp in a customs house window, a watchman's lantern moving inside the yard, a student in the shadow of a crane watching.
scene [e0e681] = 夜里的港口码头，一堵墙头插着碎玻璃的长仓库墙，海关房子的窗里一盏孤灯，院子里看守的灯笼在移动，一个学生在吊车的阴影里看着。
# en: Count the watchman's round
opt.left.label [bb126a] = 数看守的巡夜
# en: You stand in the cold under the crane till you've seen the lantern go round three times against the cathedral's clock: the long gap at the far end, the shorter one by the gate. Your feet have stopped being feet.
opt.left.say.1 [7bd60d] = 你在吊车底下的寒气里站着，对着大教堂的钟看灯笼转了三圈：远端那段长空当，大门边那段短的。你的脚已经不再是脚了。
# en: Stand the dog-man a drink
opt.right.label [b82746] = 请管狗的人喝一杯
# en: {flag(bonded_dogs_known): You stand the dog-man a drink at the harbour tavern. He's good company, and tells you how his dogs are, as if asking after old friends of yours.|You walk the dog-man to the harbour tavern and stand him a drink. He's good company, and fond of his dogs, who love him, he says sadly, and anyone else with a sausage, if you use their names. He tells you their names.}
opt.right.say.1 [9efdfd] = {flag(bonded_dogs_known): 你在港口酒馆请管狗的人喝了一杯。他是个好伴儿，跟你说起他的狗近来怎样，像在打听你的老朋友。|你陪管狗的人走到港口酒馆，请他喝了一杯。他是个好伴儿，很疼他的狗，那两条狗爱他，他伤心地说，也爱任何带着香肠、叫得出它们名字的人。他把名字告诉了你。}

@event bonded_enter
# en: Over the Wall
title [65a968] = 翻墙
# en: {job_bonded_deepest == 0: Night on the wharf. The customs' wall runs off into the dark, glass along its top, and over it the warehouse roofs, and under those the richest floor in the city: everything that's come into Port Calder and not paid its duty yet.|{&The wall, the glass along it, the customs lamp.|The wharf at night, and the wall waiting.|Over the wall, the dogs are quiet. Over the wall, the lantern goes round.}} {flag(tide_bonded_drain): You'll go in by the culvert from the tide caves tonight, which comes up under the floor.|}
text [afcf39] = {job_bonded_deepest == 0: 码头的夜。海关的墙一直伸进黑暗里，墙头插着玻璃，墙那边是仓库的屋顶，屋顶底下是全城最富的一层地板：进了考尔德港、还没缴关税的一切。|{&墙，墙头的玻璃，海关的灯。|夜里的码头，墙在等着。|墙那边，狗很安静。墙那边，灯笼一圈圈地转。}} {flag(tide_bonded_drain): 今晚你走潮汐洞窟那条涵洞进去，它通到地板底下。|}
# en: A student at night throwing a sack over the broken glass on top of a high warehouse wall, a wharf and moored ships behind, the customs lamp glowing beyond.
scene [8e005c] = 夜里一个学生把一只麻袋甩到高高的仓库墙头的碎玻璃上，身后是码头和停泊的船，远处亮着海关的灯。
# en: Not tonight
opt.left.label [4bf72b] = 今晚不了
# en: {&You leave the wall to its glass and walk home along the wharf.|Not tonight. The lantern goes round without you.|You watch a while longer and go to bed with the round still turning in your head.}
opt.left.say.1 [f4bbe6] = {&你把墙留给它的玻璃，沿着码头走回家。|今晚不了。灯笼没有你也照样转。|你又看了一会儿，上床时脑子里还转着那圈巡夜。}
# en: Go in
opt.right.label [7de3f2] = 进去
# en: A heist: press on card by card, slip away with what you carry any time.
opt.right.hint [f5be0b] = 夜盗：一张张往前走，随时可以带着手上的东西溜走。
# en: {flag(tide_bonded_drain): You go round by the tide caves and up the culvert, lift the grating between two rounds, and come up on the warehouse floor among the crates, wet to the knees.|{&You throw a sack over the glass, go over, and drop into the yard.|You go over where the glass is broken already, which somebody else found first.|You go over the wall by the crane's shadow, as quiet as you've ever been.}}
opt.right.say.1 [544606] = {flag(tide_bonded_drain): 你绕到潮汐洞窟，爬上涵洞，趁两圈巡夜之间掀开铁栅，从仓库地板的板条箱中间冒出来，膝盖以下全湿了。|{&你把麻袋甩到玻璃上，翻过去，跳进院子。|你从玻璃已经碎掉的地方翻过去，那是别人先发现的。|你借着吊车的阴影翻过墙，静得前所未有。}}

@thread job_bonded
# en: The bonded warehouses
name [4c58f4] = 保税仓库
# en: Under the crown's seal on Port Calder's wharf, the richest floor in the city waits for its duty to be paid.
premise [f1fe0c] = 在考尔德港码头的王室封印下，全城最富的一层地板等着缴清关税。
# en: You went over the customs' wall at night.
journal.1 [c30afb] = 你在夜里翻过了海关的墙。
# en: You opened the customs' strongroom.
journal.2 [fba2ad] = 你打开了海关的保险库。
# en: In the strongroom you found the foreman's private ledger, and the theft a crew boy went to gaol for.
journal.3 [99d777] = 你在保险库里找到了工头的私账，还有一个街头少年为之坐牢的那桩盗窃。
# en: You sent the foreman's ledger to the magistrate, and Jory walked out of gaol.
journal.4 [3e00b4] = 你把工头的账本送给了治安官，乔里走出了监狱。

@event bonded_dead_end
# en: No Way Through
title [4065c4] = 此路不通
# en: {job_depth >= 5: The strongroom has had all the picking it'll take tonight, and somewhere a watchman's whistle is going. The only way left is out.|{&A watchman has sat down on a crate at the end of the row with his pipe, and isn't moving. The only way that's still a way is back.|The next door's barred on the far side. Whatever's past it isn't for tonight.|A stack of tea chests has come down across the row. The noise is still going round the roof.}}
text [9b51e2] = {job_depth >= 5: 保险库今晚已经被撬够了，某处有个看守的哨子在响。只剩出去这一条路。|{&一个看守在那一排尽头的板条箱上坐下来抽烟斗，不动了。还算条路的，只有往回走。|下一扇门从那边闩上了。门后的东西不属于今晚。|一摞茶叶箱倒下来横在过道上。声响还在屋顶下回荡。}}
# en: The end of a dark warehouse row, a watchman sitting on a crate with his pipe and lantern, a student peering round a stack of tea chests.
scene [99704e] = 黑暗的仓库一排尽头，一个看守拿着烟斗和灯笼坐在板条箱上，一个学生从一摞茶叶箱后面偷看。
# en: Go back with what you carry
opt.left.label [e2014c] = 带着手上的东西回去
# en: {job_depth >= 5: You leave the iron door to the crown and go, the long way, with what you have.|{&You turn round and go by the way you know.|You take the hint, and the long way out.|You go, before anyone comes to see what fell.}}
opt.left.say.1 [a5d67f] = {job_depth >= 5: 你把铁门留给王室，带着手上的东西绕远路走了。|{&你转身走你认得的路。|你听懂了暗示，走那条长路出去。|趁没人来看是什么倒了，你走了。}}
# en: Search where you stand
opt.right.label [f7f345] = 就地搜一搜
# en: {job_depth >= 5: By the strongroom door there's a crate of seized things waiting to go in. One small one comes with you.|{&On the nearest crate the seal's already split. Something small and good comes with you.|You feel along the stack and find a packet that's fallen behind. It comes with you.|Among the fallen chests, one has burst. You fill your pockets with tea, the good kind.}}
opt.right.say.1 [b3c8f7] = {job_depth >= 5: 保险库门边有一箱等着入库的查没品。一件小的跟你走了。|{&最近的板条箱封条已经裂开了。一件又小又好的东西跟你走了。|你沿着货堆摸，找到一个掉到后面的小包。它跟你走了。|倒下的箱子里有一只摔破了。你往口袋里塞满茶叶，好茶叶。}}
# en: {job_depth >= 5: You catch your hand on the strongroom's hinge in the dark, and leave it be.|{&You find nothing but splinters.|A crate shifts under your hand, and you freeze, and leave it.|You find nothing, and bark your shin finding it.}}
opt.right.say.2 [f6d4f1] = {job_depth >= 5: 黑暗里你的手挂在保险库的门铰上，你作罢了。|{&你只找到一手木刺。|一只板条箱在你手底下挪了一下，你僵住了，作罢了。|你什么也没找到，找的时候还磕了小腿。}}

@event bonded1_dogs
# en: The Yard Dogs
title [cb9317] = 院子里的狗
# en: {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: The dogs again. One gets up, and stretches, and looks at you as if trying to remember where it's seen you.|The yard dogs are lying in the straw by the warehouse door, two of them, big as ponies in the dark. One lifts its head.} {flag(bonded_dogs_known): You know their names, and you've brought a sausage.|You don't know their names.}
text [5d6f8c] = {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: 又是那两条狗。一条站起来，伸了个懒腰，看着你，像在努力回想在哪儿见过你。|看门狗躺在仓库门边的稻草里，两条，黑暗里大得像小马。一条抬起了头。} {flag(bonded_dogs_known): 你知道它们的名字，还带了根香肠。|你不知道它们的名字。}
# en: Two big rough-coated yard dogs rising from straw by a warehouse door at night, ears up, a student frozen in the moonlit yard holding out a hand.
scene [0ae900] = 夜里两条粗毛的大看门狗从仓库门边的稻草里站起来，竖着耳朵，一个学生僵在月光下的院子里，伸着一只手。
# en: Back off over the wall
opt.left.label [bc2164] = 退回去翻出墙
# en: {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: You leave the dogs their straw. They watch you go without much interest.|You back away to the wall step by step and go over it the way you came.}
opt.left.say.1 [1811f7] = {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: 你把稻草留给狗。它们看着你走，没什么兴趣。|你一步一步退到墙边，原路翻了出去。}
# en: Walk past them like you belong
opt.right.label [27b4e5] = 像自己人一样走过去
# en: {flag(bonded_dogs_known): You say their names, softly, and hold out the sausage. Two tails go. You walk past with two large friends, who see you all the way to the door.|{seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: You walk past as if you did it every night. The dogs decide you probably do.|You walk past slow and easy, not looking at them. One sniffs your hand and lies down again.}}
opt.right.say.1 [67747b] = {flag(bonded_dogs_known): 你轻声叫出它们的名字，递出香肠。两条尾巴摇了起来。你带着两个大个子朋友走过去，它们一直把你送到门口。|{seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: 你走过去，好像每晚都这么走。狗认定你大概真是。|你不紧不慢地走过去，不看它们。一条嗅了嗅你的手，又躺下了。}}
# en: {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: The bigger dog takes your sleeve in its teeth and holds it, politely, and barks until somebody comes.|One of them barks, once, and every lantern in the yard turns your way.}
opt.right.say.2 [be927c] = {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: 大的那条叼住你的袖子，客客气气地衔着，一直叫到有人来。|其中一条叫了一声，就一声，院子里每盏灯笼都转向了你。}
# en: Step through the shadows past them
opt.up.label [08bdd2] = 借着阴影从它们身边过去
# en: {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: Shadow to shadow, past the straw. One dog sneezes. That's all.|You step into the crane's shadow and out of the shed's, twenty yards on. The dogs never stir.}
opt.up.say.1 [4824ac] = {seen(bonded1_dogs) > 1: 一片阴影接一片阴影，经过稻草堆。一条狗打了个喷嚏。仅此而已。|你踏进吊车的阴影，从二十码外棚子的阴影里出来。狗动都没动。}

@event bonded1_clerk_window
# en: The Clerk's Window
title [1f4421] = 文书的窗
# en: {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: The clerk is at his window again, working late, and the square of light lies across the yard like a rug you have to cross.|Across the yard, in the customs house, a clerk is working late: sleeve-garters, a lamp, a ledger. Between you and the warehouse door lies the square of light from his window.}
text [d0e6b4] = {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: 文书又在他的窗前加夜班，那块方形的光铺在院子里，像一块你得走过去的地毯。|院子对面的海关房子里，一个文书在加夜班：袖箍，一盏灯，一本账簿。你和仓库门之间，横着他窗户投下的那块方光。}
# en: A lit window in a customs house at night, a clerk in sleeve-garters bent over a ledger by a lamp, a dark yard outside it, a student crossing the yard in the light from the window.
scene [57462c] = 夜里海关房子一扇亮着的窗，戴袖箍的文书在灯下埋头记账，窗外是黑暗的院子，一个学生正从窗光里穿过院子。
# en: Go back over the wall
opt.left.label [acb651] = 翻墙回去
# en: {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: You go, and leave the clerk to his figures. He never looks up.|You leave him to his ledger and go back over the wall.}
opt.left.say.1 [87c184] = {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: 你走了，把文书留给他的数字。他一次也没抬头。|你把他留给他的账簿，翻墙回去了。}
# en: Walk across as if you work here
opt.right.label [a58770] = 像在这儿干活的人一样走过去
# en: {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: You cross the light whistling under your breath. The clerk raises a hand without looking. You raise one back.|You walk across his light at an honest pace, as if you'd been sent for something. He looks up, sees a shape that belongs, and looks down again.}
opt.right.say.1 [6bf40d] = {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: 你低声吹着口哨穿过那片光。文书头也不抬地举了举手。你也举了举手。|你以老实的步子穿过他的光，像是被派来取什么东西的。他抬头，看见一个像是自己人的身影，又低下了头。}
# en: {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: You hesitate in the middle of the light, which nobody who works here would do. The window goes up. "Who's that?"|He looks up, and keeps looking, and reaches for his whistle.}
opt.right.say.2 [f4cb32] = {seen(bonded1_clerk_window) > 1: 你在那片光中间犹豫了一下，在这儿干活的人谁也不会这样。窗子推开了。“谁在那儿？”|他抬起头，一直盯着，伸手去摸他的哨子。}

@event bonded1_yard_bales
# en: Bales in the Yard
title [91d648] = 院子里的货包
# en: {seen(bonded1_yard_bales) > 1: The bales in the yard again, different ones: tonight they're stamped for somewhere warm, and they smell of spice.|In the lee of the wall there are bales waiting for the morning's carts, under a tarpaulin that doesn't quite cover them. One's split, and there's bright cloth inside.}
text [0a734c] = {seen(bonded1_yard_bales) > 1: 院子里又是货包，换了一批：今晚的货印着发往某个暖和地方的字样，闻着有香料味。|墙根背风处堆着等早上装车的货包，盖着一块没盖严的油布。有一包裂了，里面是鲜亮的布料。}
# en: Bales of goods stacked under a tarpaulin in a dark warehouse yard, the sacking slit open on bright cloth, a student cutting a length free with a knife.
scene [6dd61b] = 黑暗的仓库院子里，油布下堆着货包，麻布裂开露出鲜亮的布料，一个学生用刀割下一段。
# en: Leave them and go back
opt.left.label [c117a6] = 别碰它们，回去
# en: {seen(bonded1_yard_bales) > 1: You go, and leave the spice to the carters.|You leave the bales for the morning's carts and slip back over the wall.}
opt.left.say.1 [403058] = {seen(bonded1_yard_bales) > 1: 你走了，把香料留给车夫。|你把货包留给早上的车，溜回墙那边去。}
# en: Cut a length free and go on
opt.right.label [558914] = 割一段，继续走
# en: {seen(bonded1_yard_bales) > 1: You cut a corner from a spice bale and fill your pockets, and tear a knuckle open on the bale's wire. Your eyes stream all the way to the warehouse door.|You cut a length of the bright cloth free and roll it under your coat, and slice your thumb on the sacking's wire. It's silk.}
opt.right.say.1 [de93fb] = {seen(bonded1_yard_bales) > 1: 你从一包香料上割下一角，装满口袋，被货包的铁丝划开了一个指节。你一路流着眼泪走到仓库门口。|你割下一段鲜亮的布料卷进外套里，拇指被麻包的铁丝割破了。是丝绸。}

@event bonded1_loading_door
# en: The Loading Door
title [893e00] = 装货门
# en: {seen(bonded1_loading_door) > 1: The loading door, the gap, and the ginger cat in it, who seems to have been waiting.|The warehouse's loading door has been left a hand's width open, and a ginger cat is sitting in the gap, washing.} For a moment the yard is only a yard.
text [e22176] = {seen(bonded1_loading_door) > 1: 装货门，那道缝，缝里的姜黄猫，好像一直在等着。|仓库的装货门留了一掌宽的缝，一只姜黄猫坐在缝里洗脸。} 有那么一会儿，院子只是个院子。
# en: A warehouse loading door left a hand's width open at night, a ginger cat sitting in the gap, a student crouching beside it in the dark yard.
scene [c15af9] = 夜里仓库的装货门留着一掌宽的缝，一只姜黄猫坐在缝里，一个学生蹲在黑暗的院子里它旁边。
# en: Leave it and go back
opt.left.label [8f0c89] = 不管它，回去
# en: {seen(bonded1_loading_door) > 1: You go, and the cat watches you to the wall as if you'd let it down.|You leave the cat its doorway and go back over the wall.}
opt.left.say.1 [cdb308] = {seen(bonded1_loading_door) > 1: 你走了，猫看着你一直到墙边，好像你辜负了它。|你把门口留给猫，翻墙回去了。}
# en: Slip in past the cat
opt.right.label [35441d] = 从猫身边溜进去
# en: {seen(bonded1_loading_door) > 1: You go in after the cat, who goes ahead between the crates, stopping to look back.|You slip through the gap and the cat comes with you, tail up, as if showing you round.}
opt.right.say.1 [71b6aa] = {seen(bonded1_loading_door) > 1: 你跟着猫进去，它在板条箱之间走在前面，不时停下来回头看。|你从缝里溜进去，猫竖着尾巴跟了进来，好像在带你参观。}

@event bonded2_round
# en: The Watchman's Round
title [ef5c5f] = 看守的巡夜
# en: {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: The lantern again, on the round. You know his cough now.|The floor goes on and on, crate on crate, and down the row comes the watchman's lantern on his round, slow, swinging, looking.} {flag(bonded_round_counted): You know where the round turns, and how long the gap is.|You don't know where the round goes next.}
text [2a05f9] = {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: 又是那盏灯笼，在巡夜。你现在认得他的咳嗽声了。|地板一直延伸下去，箱子叠着箱子，看守的灯笼顺着这一排巡过来，慢慢的，晃着，看着。} {flag(bonded_round_counted): 你知道巡夜在哪里转弯，空当有多长。|你不知道巡夜接下来往哪儿走。}
# en: A long warehouse floor at night between towering stacks of tea chests, a watchman's lantern coming slowly down the row, a student climbing into an empty chest.
scene [ad8f9d] = 夜里一层长长的仓库地板，茶叶箱堆得高耸，看守的灯笼沿着这一排慢慢过来，一个学生正往一只空箱子里钻。
# en: Back out while he's at the far end
opt.left.label [3744da] = 趁他在远端退出去
# en: {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: You leave the floor to the watchman and go.|You go back the way you came, behind him, step for step.}
opt.left.say.1 [4113ae] = {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: 你把地板留给看守，走了。|你跟在他后面一步一步原路回去。}
# en: Get into an empty tea chest
opt.right.label [3c61b4] = 钻进一只空茶叶箱
# en: {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: Into an empty chest, lid down, knees at your ears. The round goes by without stopping this time.|You fold yourself into an empty tea chest and pull the lid down. The lantern stops right beside it. The watchman sits on your lid, smokes half a pipe, and goes on. You come out stiff, and smelling of tea.}
opt.right.say.1 [c86950] = {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: 钻进一只空箱子，盖上盖，膝盖顶着耳朵。这回巡夜没停就过去了。|你把自己折进一只空茶叶箱，拉下盖子。灯笼就停在箱子旁边。看守坐在你的盖子上，抽了半斗烟，走了。你爬出来时浑身僵硬，一身茶味。}
# en: {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: The chest's bottom gives way under you with a crack like a shot.|The lid won't sit flat over your elbow. The lantern stops, and a hand lifts it.}
opt.right.say.2 [c8684f] = {seen(bonded2_round) > 1: 箱底在你身下咔嚓一声塌了，像开了一枪。|盖子压不平你的胳膊肘。灯笼停下来，一只手掀开了它。}

@event bonded2_seals
# en: The Crown's Seals
title [e28c03] = 王室的封印
# en: {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: The silk under the crown's seals again, a new cargo of it. The wax is fresh.|Here the silk is, the best of the floor: bales corded and sealed with red wax and the crown, every one. Break a seal and the morning shift will know by breakfast.}
text [b40fa2] = {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: 王室封印下的丝绸又来了一批新货。蜡还是新的。|丝绸在这儿，整层地板上最好的货：一包包都捆着绳、封着印着王冠的红蜡。弄破一个封印，早班的人吃早饭前就会知道。}
# en: Bales of silk on a warehouse floor at night, each corded and fixed with a red wax customs seal stamped with a crown, a student working a thin knife under one of the seals.
scene [328958] = 夜里仓库地板上的丝绸包，每包都捆着绳、封着印有王冠的红色海关蜡封，一个学生把一把薄刀插到一个封印底下。
# en: Leave the seals and go back
opt.left.label [620b59] = 别碰封印，回去
# en: {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: You go back the way you came, and the seals stay whole.|You leave the crown its wax and go.}
opt.left.say.1 [62a431] = {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: 你原路回去，封印完好无损。|你把蜡留给王室，走了。}
# en: Lift a seal without breaking it
opt.right.label [6648fa] = 揭起封印而不弄破
# en: {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: You lift the seal with a hot knife, take your silk and put it back. It's horribly easy, which you try not to think about.|You warm the knife in your hand and slide it under the wax, slow as a clock, and the seal lifts whole. You take two lengths and press the wax back. Nobody will know till the bale's weighed.}
opt.right.say.1 [df1ee8] = {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: 你用热刀揭起封印，拿了丝绸，再把它放回去。容易得吓人，你尽量不去想。|你把刀在手里焐热，慢得像钟表一样插到蜡下面，封印完整地揭了起来。你拿了两段，又把蜡按回去。不到称重谁也不会知道。}
# en: {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: The knife slips and the cord parts and the whole bale slumps open across the floor.|The wax cracks in half with a noise like a shot, in the silence.}
opt.right.say.2 [e8e8c1] = {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: 刀一滑，绳子断了，整包货在地板上瘫开。|一片寂静里，蜡裂成两半，响得像开了一枪。}
# en: Cut it, take it, seal it again
opt.up.label [39ccb2] = 割开，拿走，再封上
# en: {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: You take your silk and seal the bale behind you, neater than the customs did.|You cut the cord, take two lengths, and close the bale again with a word. The wax flows back together, crown and all. The crown will never know.}
opt.up.say.1 [bc55f3] = {seen(bonded2_seals) > 1: 你拿了丝绸，在身后把货包封好，比海关封得还整齐。|你割断绳子，拿了两段，念一个词把货包重新封上。蜡流回原处，王冠也在。王室永远不会知道。}

@event bonded2_crane_loft
# en: The Crane Gantry
title [5c7d64] = 吊车轨架
# en: {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: The gantry again. Somebody's left a hook swinging on its chain, slowly, as if somebody had just gone by.|The quick way across the floor is overhead: the iron gantry the cranes run on, under the roof, with chains and hooks hanging from it into the dark.}
text [c62a69] = {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: 又是轨架。有人留了一只钩子在链子上慢慢地晃，好像刚有人经过。|穿过地板最快的路在头顶：屋顶下吊车跑的铁轨架，链子和钩子垂进黑暗里。}
# en: An iron crane gantry running high under a warehouse roof at night, chains and hooks hanging, a student edging along it above a dark floor of crates.
scene [a8f970] = 夜里仓库屋顶下高高的铁制吊车轨架，挂着链子和钩子，一个学生沿着它挪过黑暗的板条箱地面上方。
# en: Stay on the ground and go back
opt.left.label [275b11] = 待在地上，回去
# en: {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: You go back. The hook goes on swinging.|You leave the gantry to the pigeons and go back the long way, on the ground.}
opt.left.say.1 [d7e993] = {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: 你回去了。钩子还在晃。|你把轨架留给鸽子，在地上绕远路回去。}
# en: Go along the gantry
opt.right.label [4399f4] = 沿着轨架过去
# en: {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: You cross on the iron, quick and quiet, and drop down past the round without it knowing.|You go along the gantry hand over hand, over the whole floor and the watchman's lantern, and drop down by the far wall soft as a cat.}
opt.right.say.1 [f7f205] = {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: 你在铁架上又快又静地过去，从巡夜的头顶落下，它毫无察觉。|你手攀手沿着轨架过去，越过整层地板和看守的灯笼，在远处的墙边像猫一样轻轻落地。}
# en: {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: You slip, and hang by your hands, and when you drop the crate you land on goes over.|A chain swings into you and its hook rings off the iron like a gong, over the whole floor.}
opt.right.say.2 [a15046] = {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: 你一滑，吊在半空，松手落下时踩翻了脚下的板条箱。|一根链子荡过来撞上你，钩子敲在铁架上像敲锣，响遍整层地板。}
# en: Run it
opt.up.label [430853] = 跑过去
# en: {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: You run the iron, quick as thought. The pigeons don't even wake.|You go faster than the gantry can creak, the length of the roof in a breath, and drop down at the far wall.}
opt.up.say.1 [25ec7c] = {seen(bonded2_crane_loft) > 1: 你在铁架上跑，快如念头。鸽子都没醒。|你跑得比轨架嘎吱响得还快，一口气跑完屋顶，在远处墙边落下。}

@event bonded2_spirit_floor
# en: The Spirit Floor
title [c6e3cb] = 烈酒层
# en: {seen(bonded2_spirit_floor) > 1: The spirit floor again. The fumes are worse tonight; somebody's cask is weeping.|The spirit floor: casks of rum and brandy racked to the roof, every one with the crown burned into its head, and the air so thick with fumes your eyes water.}
text [a329e8] = {seen(bonded2_spirit_floor) > 1: 又是烈酒层。今晚酒气更重了；有个桶在渗。|烈酒层：朗姆和白兰地的桶一直码到屋顶，每个桶头都烙着王冠，空气里的酒气浓得你眼睛流泪。}
# en: Rows of great casks of rum and brandy on racks in a dark warehouse, a student drawing spirit from a cask through a gimlet hole into a flask, coughing at the fumes.
scene [a6e815] = 黑暗仓库里一排排架子上的朗姆和白兰地大桶，一个学生从桶上的钻孔往小酒壶里放酒，被酒气呛得直咳。
# en: Hold your breath and go back
opt.left.label [35ae3f] = 屏住气回去
# en: {seen(bonded2_spirit_floor) > 1: You leave the casks to the crown and go, eyes streaming.|You go back, breathing through your sleeve.}
opt.left.say.1 [ec241f] = {seen(bonded2_spirit_floor) > 1: 你把酒桶留给王室，走了，眼泪直流。|你隔着袖子呼吸，回去了。}
# en: Fill two flasks and go on
opt.right.label [2d172c] = 灌两壶，继续走
# en: {seen(bonded2_spirit_floor) > 1: You fill your flasks from the rum. Your head swims for the length of the floor.|You bore a hole low in a brandy cask, fill two flasks, and stop it with a peg. The fumes go straight to your head, and you walk on a little wider than you meant to.}
opt.right.say.1 [f43dcc] = {seen(bonded2_spirit_floor) > 1: 你从朗姆桶里灌满了酒壶。走完这一层，你的头一直在晕。|你在一只白兰地桶底部钻了个孔，灌满两壶，用木塞堵上。酒气直冲脑门，你往前走时步子比想的宽了些。}

@event bonded2_tea_floor
# en: The Tea Floor
title [80c8c0] = 茶叶层
# en: {seen(bonded2_tea_floor) > 1: The tea floor, and the dust, and the lantern at the end of the row. Your nose remembers.|The tea floor: chests stacked to the roof, and tea dust hanging in the dark so fine you can feel it in your nose. At the end of the row the lantern's coming.}
text [76376f] = {seen(bonded2_tea_floor) > 1: 茶叶层，灰尘，还有这一排尽头的灯笼。你的鼻子记得。|茶叶层：箱子码到屋顶，茶灰悬在黑暗里，细得你能在鼻子里感觉到。这一排尽头，灯笼过来了。}
# en: Tea chests stacked to the roof of a dark warehouse floor, fine dust in the air, a student holding their nose to stop a sneeze while a lantern passes at the end of the row.
scene [19a14f] = 黑暗仓库里茶叶箱码到屋顶，空气里飘着细灰，一个学生捏着鼻子忍住喷嚏，一盏灯笼从这一排尽头经过。
# en: Back out before you sneeze
opt.left.label [affca0] = 趁打喷嚏之前退出去
# en: {seen(bonded2_tea_floor) > 1: You go, holding your nose, and sneeze into the river.|You back out with your sleeve over your face and get as far as the wharf before you sneeze.}
opt.left.say.1 [0d853c] = {seen(bonded2_tea_floor) > 1: 你捏着鼻子走了，冲着河打了个喷嚏。|你用袖子捂着脸退出去，一直到码头才打出喷嚏。}
# en: Fill your pockets and hold it in
opt.right.label [2c453a] = 装满口袋，忍住
# en: {seen(bonded2_tea_floor) > 1: You take your tea and fight your nose all the way down the row. Your nose nearly wins.|You fill your pockets with the best tea in Port Calder and stand absolutely still, eyes streaming, through the whole of the lantern going by. It's the longest minute of your life.}
opt.right.say.1 [af5883] = {seen(bonded2_tea_floor) > 1: 你拿了茶叶，一路和自己的鼻子较劲走完这一排。鼻子差点赢了。|你往口袋里装满考尔德港最好的茶叶，一动不动地站着，眼泪直流，熬过灯笼经过的整段时间。这是你这辈子最长的一分钟。}

@event bonded_strongroom
# en: The Crown's Strongroom
title [9dbe17] = 王室保险库
# en: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: The strongroom's iron door again, the crown on it, the same padlock.|At the end of the floor, behind an iron door with the crown cast on it, is the customs' strongroom: everything the crown has seized, waiting for auction. The padlock is the size of your two fists.} {flag(bonded_strongroom): You've had it open before.|}
text [b2a7f0] = {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: 又是保险库的铁门，上面的王冠，同一把挂锁。|地板尽头，一扇铸着王冠的铁门后面是海关的保险库：王室查没的一切，等着拍卖。挂锁有你两个拳头那么大。} {flag(bonded_strongroom): 你以前打开过它。|}
# en: A heavy iron door with a crown cast on it at the end of a dark warehouse floor, a big padlock, a student kneeling at the lock with a lantern shaded under their coat.
scene [e7991a] = 黑暗仓库地板尽头一扇铸着王冠的沉重铁门，一把大挂锁，一个学生跪在锁前，外套底下遮着一盏灯。
# en: Leave it and get out
opt.left.label [25b9d8] = 别碰它，出去
# en: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: You leave the crown its strongroom and go while the round's at the far end.|You leave the iron door alone and go, by the long way, with what you have.}
opt.left.say.1 [bab835] = {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: 你把保险库留给王室，趁巡夜在远端时走了。|你没碰那扇铁门，带着手上的东西绕远路走了。}
# en: Work the padlock
opt.right.label [6234b1] = 对付那把挂锁
# en: {flag(bonded_strongroom): The padlock gives again. Inside, the seized goods have changed, and the pick of them comes with you.|The padlock gives with a sound like a cough. Inside, on shelves: seized jewellery, a case of duelling pistols, bolts of contraband lace, and a drawer nobody has locked.}
opt.right.say.1 [03c812] = {flag(bonded_strongroom): 挂锁又开了。里面的查没品换了，最好的几样跟你走了。|挂锁咳嗽似的响了一声，开了。里面的架子上：查没的首饰，一箱决斗手枪，几匹走私的蕾丝，还有一个没上锁的抽屉。}
# en: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: The padlock won't move, and you work at it too long. The round comes back early.|The pick snaps in the lock, and the iron door booms when you knock it, and a whistle answers.}
opt.right.say.2 [ad2b88] = {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: 挂锁纹丝不动，你弄得太久了。巡夜提前回来了。|撬针在锁里断了，你碰到铁门时它嗡地一响，一声哨子应了过来。}
# en: Pick it with the proper tools
opt.up.label [f35e05] = 用正经工具撬
# en: {flag(bonded_strongroom): Eleven picks, and you know which one now. The door opens on the crown's newest seizures.|Eleven picks and a tension wrench, and the padlock opens on the fourth. Inside, on shelves: seized jewellery, a case of duelling pistols, bolts of contraband lace, and a drawer nobody has locked.}
opt.up.say.1 [6ed246] = {flag(bonded_strongroom): 十一根撬针，你现在知道是哪一根了。门开了，里面是王室最新的查没品。|十一根撬针加一把张力扳手，挂锁在第四根上开了。里面的架子上：查没的首饰，一箱决斗手枪，几匹走私的蕾丝，还有一个没上锁的抽屉。}
# en: {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: Even with the proper picks the old lock fights you, and the round comes back before it gives.|The fourth pick bends, then the fifth, and while you fumble for the sixth a whistle goes at the end of the floor.}
opt.up.say.2 [012658] = {seen(bonded_strongroom) > 1: 就算用正经的撬针，那把老锁也跟你较劲，它还没开，巡夜就回来了。|第四根撬针弯了，接着是第五根，你摸第六根时，这层地板尽头响起了哨子。}

@event bonded_ledger
# en: The Foreman's Ledger
title [f0e921] = 工头的账本
# en: In the unlocked drawer there's a ledger in the warehouse foreman's hand. Two columns for every cargo: what came in, and what the crown was told came in. The difference goes out by a side door, month after month. One night is circled: a crate gone that the foreman had sold already, {has(origin_street): and Jory caught on the floor that night with nothing in his hands, and sent down for the lot.|and a young man from one of Port Calder's street crews, caught on the floor that night, sent to gaol for the lot.}
text [eb666f] = 没上锁的抽屉里有一本账簿，是仓库工头的笔迹。每批货两栏：进了多少，报给王室进了多少。差额从一扇侧门出去，月复一月。有一夜被圈了出来：丢了一箱工头早就卖掉的货，{has(origin_street): 那晚乔里两手空空地在地板上被抓，替整批货坐了牢。|那晚一个考尔德港街头帮伙的年轻人在地板上被抓，替整批货进了监狱。}
# en: A student in a dark strongroom reading a ledger by a shaded lantern, two columns of figures in the same hand, a page with a date circled.
scene [0febe7] = 黑暗的保险库里，一个学生借着遮光灯读一本账簿，同一个笔迹的两栏数字，一页上圈着一个日期。
# en: Send it to the magistrate
opt.left.label [44328d] = 把它送给治安官
# en: Before dawn you leave the ledger wrapped in oilcloth on the magistrate's own doorstep, unsigned. Within the week the foreman's in the cells{has(origin_street): and Jory's out of them, blinking at the daylight on the loft step.|, and the young crew boy who took his blame walks out of gaol.} Nobody knows who sent it. You lose the ledger's price, and don't miss it.
opt.left.say.1 [9b2cea] = 天亮前你把账本用油布包好，放在治安官自家门阶上，不署名。不到一周工头就进了牢房{has(origin_street): ，乔里出来了，在阁楼台阶上对着天光眨眼。|，替他背黑锅的那个帮伙少年走出了监狱。}没人知道是谁送的。你丢了账本能卖的价钱，并不心疼。
# en: Sell it back to the foreman
opt.right.label [149b97] = 把它卖回给工头
# en: You send the foreman one page of his own ledger and a time. He comes alone, pays in gold without a word, and burns the book in front of you. {has(origin_street): Jory stays where he is.|The crew boy who took his blame stays where he is.} The gold is heavy in your pocket all the way home.
opt.right.say.1 [90c44f] = 你给工头送去他自己账本的一页，约了个时间。他一个人来，一言不发地付了金子，当着你的面烧了账本。{has(origin_street): 乔里还待在原地。|替他背黑锅的那个帮伙少年还待在原地。}一路回家，口袋里的金子沉甸甸的。

@event crew_loft_jory_home
# en: Jory Home
title [386a16] = 乔里回家
# en: {seen(crew_loft_empty_hammock) > 0: The empty hammock isn't empty. Jory's in it, thinner,|There's a face in the loft you know only from the foreman's ledger: Jory, back from a year in the city gaol, in his own hammock, thinner,} with a bowl of soup and the whole loft finding reasons to walk past him. "Somebody sent the magistrate a book," he tells you. "Nobody knows who." Across the stove Nan Merrow looks at you once, and goes back to dealing.
text [b35b44] = {seen(crew_loft_empty_hammock) > 0: 那张空吊床不空了。乔里躺在里面，瘦了，|阁楼里有一张你只在工头账本上见过的面孔：乔里，在城里监狱待了一年回来了，躺在自己的吊床里，瘦了，}捧着一碗汤，整个阁楼的人都找着理由从他身边走过。“有人给治安官寄了本书，”他告诉你，“没人知道是谁。”炉子对面，南·梅罗看了你一眼，又接着发牌。
# en: A harbour-town loft with a row of hammocks, a thin young man sitting up in one eating soup, a sharp-eyed older woman and a student at the stove, the crew round a card table.
scene [f9ae4f] = 港城的一间阁楼，一排吊床，一个瘦削的年轻人坐在其中一张里喝汤，炉边一个目光锐利的年长女人和一个学生，伙伴们围着牌桌。
# en: Stand the loft a round
opt.left.label [a0dc18] = 请全阁楼喝一轮
# en: You buy the loft a round, and then another, and Jory tells the whole room about the gaol's food till they beg him to stop. Nan says nothing at all to you all night, which in the loft is the highest thing she has to give.
opt.left.say.1 [68f957] = 你请全阁楼喝了一轮，又一轮，乔里给满屋子人讲监狱的伙食，讲到他们求他别说了。南整晚一句话也没对你说，在阁楼里这是她能给的最高的东西。
# en: Sit with Jory a while
opt.right.label [11758f] = 陪乔里坐一会儿
# en: You sit up with Jory by the stove till the small hours, talking about nothing, while he eats everything in reach. In the morning he's asleep in his own hammock for the first time in a year, and you're grey with tiredness.
opt.right.say.1 [6a25fc] = 你陪乔里在炉边坐到后半夜，聊些有的没的，他把够得着的东西全吃了。早上他一年来头一回睡在自己的吊床里，你累得脸色发灰。

@event club_gala_card
# en: An Invitation, Not Yours
title [cc342e] = 一张不属于你的请柬
# en: Down the side of a club armchair, among the crumbs and a lost glove, there's a stiff gilt-edged card: an invitation to a ball at the tallest house on the Crescent, this week and every week he's in town, "and guest". The name on it belongs to a member snoring in the next chair.
text [47a4d1] = 俱乐部一把扶手椅的侧缝里，面包屑和一只丢了的手套中间，夹着一张硬挺的烫金卡片：新月街最高那幢宅子的舞会请柬，本周以及主人在城里的每一周，“可携一位客人”。上面的名字属于隔壁椅子上正打着呼噜的会员。
# en: A members' club's leather armchair, a stiff gilt-edged invitation card fallen down between the cushions, a student holding it up to the lamp.
scene [3981aa] = 会员俱乐部的皮扶手椅，一张硬挺的烫金请柬掉在坐垫之间，一个学生把它举到灯下。
# en: Keep it
opt.left.label [87c2f5] = 留着它
# en: You put it in your pocket. The member snores on. It's only a card, you tell yourself, and he has a hundred; you feel it in your pocket all the way home, like a stone.
opt.left.say.1 [2b7ccc] = 你把它放进口袋。那位会员还在打呼噜。不过是张卡片，你对自己说，他有上百张；一路回家，你都觉得口袋里像揣着块石头。
# en: Wake him and give it back
opt.right.label [d0144b] = 叫醒他，还给他
# en: You wake him. He's furious at being woken, then delighted about the card, then furious again, and tells you all about the house: a shipowner's, new money, a safe in the study "the size of a wardrobe", he says, as if that were vulgar. You leave without even a thank-you.
opt.right.say.1 [69b601] = 你叫醒他。他先是气被吵醒，接着为卡片高兴，然后又生气了，把那幢宅子的事全告诉了你：一个船东的，暴发户，书房里有个保险柜“大得像衣柜”，他说得好像那很粗俗。你走的时候连句谢谢都没得到。

@event undercroft_crescent_tip
# en: The Shipowner's Safe
title [210a0c] = 船东的保险柜
# en: The fence in the velvet waistcoat beckons you to his alcove. "A word, academy. The tallest house on the Crescent. A shipowner, new money, a ball every week he's in town and a safe in the study that the whole of Port Calder paid for, one way and another." He polishes his loupe. "I'd pay well for anything in it. Only saying."
text [d6c9a1] = 那个穿天鹅绒背心的销赃人招手叫你去他的凹室。“说句话，学院的。新月街最高那幢宅子。一个船东，暴发户，他在城里时每周开一场舞会，书房里有个保险柜，整个考尔德港都为它掏过钱，这样那样的。”他擦着放大镜。“里面的东西，我出好价钱。只是说说。”
# en: A fence in a velvet waistcoat in a candlelit cellar alcove, leaning across his table of watches and rings to speak low to a student, a jeweller's loupe in his eye.
scene [52b760] = 烛光映照的地窖凹室里，一个穿天鹅绒背心、戴着珠宝放大镜的销赃人隔着摆满怀表和戒指的桌子，低声对一个学生说话。
# en: Ask him how you'd get in
opt.left.label [9a6bd1] = 问他怎么进去
# en: "During the ball," he says, "everybody's somebody. The servants' door's on the mews, and the servants change over at eleven." He doesn't charge for it. That's how you know he means it.
opt.left.say.1 [01ff22] = “舞会的时候，”他说，“人人都是个人物。仆人的门在马厩巷，仆人十一点换班。”这条消息他没收钱。你由此知道他是认真的。
# en: Say you'll think about it
opt.right.label [b4769e] = 说你会考虑考虑
# en: "Do," he says, and smiles, and goes back to his loupe as if you'd already said yes. "Eleven o'clock," he adds, to the watch he's mending. "The mews door." You walk out knowing exactly which house he meant, and that he knows you know, which sits badly with you all night.
opt.right.say.1 [41af3a] = “考虑吧，”他说着笑了笑，回去摆弄放大镜，好像你已经答应了。“十一点，”他对着正在修的怀表补了一句，“马厩巷那扇门。”你走出去时清楚地知道他说的是哪幢宅子，也知道他知道你知道，这让你整晚都不舒服。

@event crescent_gala_lights
# en: The Ball on the Crescent
title [0865c4] = 新月街的舞会
# en: {seen(crescent_gala_lights) > 1: The ball again, the carriages, the music. A footman on the steps is turning people away, politely, with his whole face, and a link-boy with a torch is sitting on the railings beside you, waiting for his gentleman.|The tallest house on the Crescent is lit from cellar to attic. Carriages queue round the curve, {season == "winter": breath steaming from the horses,|the summer dusk still warm,} and from the tall windows comes music and the noise of money enjoying itself. A link-boy with a torch sits on the gardens' railings beside you.}
text [9d6924] = {seen(crescent_gala_lights) > 1: 又是舞会，马车，音乐。台阶上一个男仆正客客气气地、用整张脸把人往外挡，一个举着火把的引路童坐在你旁边的栏杆上，等他的主人。|新月街最高那幢宅子从地窖到阁楼灯火通明。马车沿着弧形街排成长队，{season == "winter": 马匹呼着白气，|夏日的黄昏还是暖的，}高高的窗子里传出音乐和金钱寻欢作乐的声响。一个举着火把的引路童坐在你旁边花园的栏杆上。}
# en: A tall lit-up town house on a curving terrace at night, carriages drawing up, music and figures behind tall windows, a student watching from the railings of the gardens opposite.
scene [a45a4c] = 夜里弧形排屋中一幢灯火通明的高宅，马车停靠，高窗后人影和音乐，一个学生在对面花园的栏杆边看着。
# en: Count the windows and the doors
opt.left.label [6c9eb5] = 数窗户和门
# en: You stand at the gardens' railings until you know every window, the mews door, the footmen (too many), and which room upstairs is the study. {season == "winter": Your hands have gone numb and your feet ache.|The midges have had you for supper and your feet ache.}
opt.left.say.1 [a67d55] = 你在花园栏杆边站着，直到摸清每一扇窗、马厩巷的门、男仆（太多了），还有楼上哪间是书房。{season == "winter": 你的手冻麻了，脚也酸了。|蠓虫拿你当了晚饭，脚也酸了。}
# en: Pay the link-boy for the servants' hour
opt.right.label [d85dcc] = 付钱给引路童，打听仆人换班
# en: {flag(crescent_servants_hour): You give the link-boy a coin for his company. He tells you the cook's name and the dog's, and the house's whole week of scandal, and you already know about the mews door at eleven.|You give the link-boy a coin for his torch and his gossip. The servants change over at eleven, he says; the mews door stands open for the trays.}
opt.right.say.1 [97dbab] = {flag(crescent_servants_hour): 你给了引路童一枚硬币，就为他陪你说话。他告诉你厨娘的名字、狗的名字，还有这家整整一周的丑闻，至于十一点马厩巷的门，你早知道了。|你给了引路童一枚硬币，换他的火把光和闲话。仆人十一点换班，他说；马厩巷的门开着让托盘进出。}

@event crescent_enter
# en: Everybody's Somebody
title [37b80a] = 人人都是个人物
# en: {job_crescent_deepest == 0: Tonight the tallest house on the Crescent is giving its ball, and during a ball everybody's somebody. Upstairs, past the ballroom and the guests on the stairs, there's a study with a safe the size of a wardrobe.|{&The ball again, and the music, and the study upstairs.|Carriages at the door, the mews door open for the trays.|The tall house, lit up, and the safe waiting.}} {flag(crescent_invited): You've a gilt card that says "and guest".|You'll need a way in.}
text [58e685] = {job_crescent_deepest == 0: 今晚新月街最高那幢宅子在开舞会，舞会上人人都是个人物。楼上，过了舞厅和楼梯上的客人，有间书房，里面有个大得像衣柜的保险柜。|{&又是舞会，音乐，楼上的书房。|门口的马车，马厩巷的门开着让托盘进出。|那幢高宅，灯火通明，保险柜在等着。}} {flag(crescent_invited): 你有一张写着“可携一位客人”的烫金卡片。|你得想个办法进去。}
# en: A student in borrowed evening clothes slipping in through a lit doorway among elegant guests in silks and jewels, a grand staircase and chandeliers inside.
scene [d90d85] = 一个穿着借来的晚礼服的学生混在穿丝绸戴珠宝的优雅客人中间，溜进一扇灯火通明的门，里面是宏伟的楼梯和枝形吊灯。
# en: Not tonight
opt.left.label [4bf72b] = 今晚不了
# en: {&You leave the ball to its guests and walk home under the gardens' trees.|Not tonight. The music follows you down the hill.|You watch the carriages a while longer, and go.}
opt.left.say.1 [c1d0c0] = {&你把舞会留给客人们，在花园的树下走回家。|今晚不了。音乐一路跟着你下了山。|你又看了一会儿马车，走了。}
# en: Go in
opt.right.label [7de3f2] = 进去
# en: A heist: press on card by card, slip away with what you carry any time.
opt.right.hint [f5be0b] = 夜盗：一张张往前走，随时可以带着手上的东西溜走。
# en: {flag(crescent_invited): You hand the footman your gilt card, and he bows you in under the chandeliers as somebody's guest.|{flag(crescent_servants_hour): At eleven you go in by the mews door behind a tray of ices, as if you'd carried one all your life.|You go in on the tail of a noisy party from a carriage, laughing at nothing, as if you belonged to it.}}
opt.right.say.1 [e3f626] = {flag(crescent_invited): 你把烫金卡片递给男仆，他躬身把你作为某人的客人迎进枝形吊灯底下。|{flag(crescent_servants_hour): 十一点，你跟在一盘冰淇淋后面从马厩巷的门进去，好像你这辈子一直在端托盘。|你跟在一辆马车下来的一群吵吵嚷嚷的人后面进去，莫名其妙地笑着，好像你是他们一伙的。}}

@thread job_crescent
# en: The house on the Crescent
name [e5fa55] = 新月街的宅子
# en: The tallest house on the Crescent gives a ball every week its owner is in town, and has a safe in the study the size of a wardrobe.
premise [f7eec5] = 新月街最高那幢宅子在主人进城的每一周都开舞会，书房里有个大得像衣柜的保险柜。
# en: You went into the ball on the Crescent with nobody's invitation.
journal.1 [41d9b7] = 你没有请柬，进了新月街的舞会。
# en: In the shipowner's writing desk you read his letters to a warehouse foreman on the wharf.
journal.2 [a87406] = 你在船东的写字台里读了他写给码头上一个仓库工头的信。
# en: You opened the safe in the shipowner's study.
journal.3 [f8e7d3] = 你打开了船东书房里的保险柜。

@event crescent_dead_end
# en: The Music Stops
title [d4767a] = 音乐停了
# en: {job_depth >= 5: The safe has had all the listening it'll bear tonight, and somebody's coming up the stairs with a lamp. The only way left is down.|{&The butler has taken up a post at the top of the stairs and isn't moving. The only way that's still a way is down.|The music stops for a speech, and every face in the house turns your way. Not tonight.|A door along the landing is locked, and voices behind the next one. Whatever's further on isn't for tonight.}}
text [c0dc93] = {job_depth >= 5: 保险柜今晚已经被听够了，有人提着灯上楼来了。只剩下楼这一条路。|{&管家在楼梯顶上站定，不动了。还算条路的，只有往下。|音乐停下来听一段致辞，满屋子的脸都转向你这边。今晚不行。|楼道前面一扇门锁着，下一扇门后有人说话。再往前的东西不属于今晚。}}
# en: A grand staircase in a lit town house, a stern butler standing at the top of it with his hands behind his back, a student halfway up in evening clothes.
scene [b4d6bd] = 灯火通明的宅子里一道宏伟的楼梯，一个神情严厉的管家背着手站在楼梯顶，一个穿晚礼服的学生站在半截。
# en: Go with what you carry
opt.left.label [3cefe9] = 带着手上的东西走
# en: {job_depth >= 5: You leave the safe and go down the back stairs with what you have.|{&You turn and go down among the guests, and out with a crowd that's leaving.|You take the hint, and your coat, and go.|You go down the back stairs, past a maid who doesn't look up.}}
opt.left.say.1 [43fb82] = {job_depth >= 5: 你丢下保险柜，带着手上的东西从后楼梯下去了。|{&你转身混进客人中间下楼，跟着一群正要走的人出去了。|你听懂了暗示，拿上外套走了。|你从后楼梯下去，经过一个头也不抬的女仆。}}
# en: Look about where you stand
opt.right.label [db755b] = 就地看看
# en: {job_depth >= 5: On the study's mantel there's a little gold snuffbox nobody will count tonight. It comes with you.|{&On a side table a guest has left a gold cigar case. It comes with you.|In the crush a pearl drops from somebody's earring. You pick it up, and keep it.|A silver card tray, with nobody's eye on it. It comes with you.}}
opt.right.say.1 [d12cf1] = {job_depth >= 5: 书房壁炉台上有个小小的金鼻烟盒，今晚没人会数。它跟你走了。|{&边桌上一位客人落下了一个金雪茄盒。它跟你走了。|人挤人时，谁的耳环上掉下一颗珍珠。你捡了起来，留下了。|一只银名片盘，没人盯着。它跟你走了。}}
# en: {job_depth >= 5: A maid comes in to see to the fire, and you have to admire the clock for a long minute, and leave empty-handed.|{&A footman watches your hands the whole time. You leave them in your pockets.|A guest catches your eye and keeps it. You smile, and touch nothing.|You find nothing worth the risk, and a dowager's stare.}}
opt.right.say.2 [372960] = {job_depth >= 5: 一个女仆进来照看炉火，你只好欣赏了好一会儿钟，空着手离开。|{&一个男仆一直盯着你的手。你把手放在口袋里。|一位客人和你对上了眼，就不放开了。你笑了笑，什么也没碰。|你没找到值得冒险的东西，只换来一位老夫人的瞪视。}}

@event crescent1_footman
# en: The Footman's Eye
title [04c0d3] = 男仆的眼睛
# en: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: The same footman at the ballroom doors, the same moment too long.|At the ballroom doors a footman in a powdered wig looks at every guest as they pass, and at you a moment longer.}
text [26c6c9] = {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: 舞厅门口还是那个男仆，还是多看的那一眼。|舞厅门口，一个戴扑粉假发的男仆打量着每一位经过的客人，看你的时候多看了一眼。}
# en: A tall footman in powdered wig and livery at the door of a ballroom, looking down his nose at a student in evening clothes, dancers whirling beyond.
scene [5eb6c0] = 舞厅门口一个戴扑粉假发、穿号衣的高个男仆，居高临下地看着一个穿晚礼服的学生，里面的舞者在旋转。
# en: Back out into the night
opt.left.label [189a0d] = 退回夜色里
# en: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: You leave the footman to his doors and go home.|You turn back as if you'd forgotten your gloves, and keep going, out of the house.}
opt.left.say.1 [886acd] = {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: 你把门留给男仆，回家了。|你转身，好像忘了手套，一直走出了宅子。}
# en: Look as if you belong
opt.right.label [fbe0a1] = 装作本就属于这里
# en: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: You walk past him talking over your shoulder to nobody about the terrible music. He bows you through.|You give him the faint, bored smile of somebody who has been to a great many of these. He bows, slightly. You're in.}
opt.right.say.1 [52ea3e] = {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: 你从他身边走过，回头跟不存在的人抱怨着糟糕的音乐。他躬身让你过去。|你给了他一个淡淡的、厌倦的笑，像是参加过许多场这样的舞会。他微微一躬。你进去了。}
# en: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: He steps across the doorway, very politely, and doesn't step back.|"Your name, sir or madam?" he asks, in a voice that carries.}
opt.right.say.2 [70f827] = {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: 他非常客气地横跨一步挡住门口，再也不退回去。|“请问您贵姓，先生还是女士？”他问，声音传得老远。}
# en: Charm him
opt.up.label [94e33a] = 迷住他
# en: {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: He remembers liking you, and not quite why. He bows.|You smile at him with a little more charm than you have, and he finds himself remembering you from last week. He bows you in.}
opt.up.say.1 [038772] = {seen(crescent1_footman) > 1: 他记得自己喜欢你，又说不清为什么。他躬身。|你带着比实际多一点的魅力冲他一笑，他发现自己记得上周见过你。他躬身迎你进去。}

@event crescent1_quadrille
# en: A Partner for the Quadrille
title [dfe54f] = 方阵舞的舞伴
# en: {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: The old lady in diamonds again, and the quadrille again. "You," she says. "Come along."|An old lady in diamonds takes your arm with surprising strength. "You'll do," she says. "My nephew's vanished, and the quadrille's starting." The dance would take you the length of the ballroom, to the foot of the stairs.}
text [0656c4] = {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: 又是那位戴钻石的老夫人，又是方阵舞。“你，”她说，“过来。”|一位戴钻石的老夫人以惊人的力气挽住你的胳膊。“你就行，”她说，“我侄子不见了，方阵舞要开始了。”这支舞会把你带过整个舞厅，一直到楼梯脚下。}
# en: A chandeliered ballroom, couples forming up in squares for a dance, an elderly lady in diamonds taking a student's arm firmly, the student glancing toward a staircase.
scene [40c9e1] = 枝形吊灯下的舞厅，一对对舞伴排成方阵准备跳舞，一位戴钻石的老夫人紧紧挽住一个学生的胳膊，学生瞟着楼梯。
# en: Make your excuses and slip out
opt.left.label [f55be9] = 找个借口溜出去
# en: {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: You tell her you've promised the dance. She snorts. You go.|You plead a turned ankle and limp out of the house, convincingly, all the way down the hill.}
opt.left.say.1 [dc2131] = {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: 你告诉她这支舞已经答应了别人。她哼了一声。你走了。|你推说扭了脚踝，一瘸一拐地走出宅子，装得很像，一直瘸到山下。}
# en: Dance her down the room
opt.right.label [675449] = 领着她跳过整个舞厅
# en: {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: You get through the quadrille without disgrace, and she lets go of you by the stairs. "Nearly adequate," she says.|You get the figures right, mostly, and she's delighted, and leaves you at the foot of the stairs with a rap of her fan and the word "adequate". Nobody sees you go up.}
opt.right.say.1 [401da6] = {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: 你总算没丢脸地跳完了方阵舞，她在楼梯边放开了你。“差不多算合格，”她说。|你大致跳对了舞步，她很高兴，在楼梯脚下用扇子敲了你一下，说了句“合格”就放开了你。没人看见你上楼。}
# en: {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: You tread on her train, and the diamonds go everywhere, and so do the eyes of the room.|You go left when the whole square goes right, and walk her into the host. Everybody's looking at you now.}
opt.right.say.2 [f8455b] = {seen(crescent1_quadrille) > 1: 你踩住了她的裙裾，钻石散了一地，满屋子的目光也一样。|整个方阵往右，你往左，把她领着撞上了主人。现在所有人都在看你。}

@event crescent1_supper_table
# en: The Supper Table
title [5eed9f] = 夜宵桌
# en: {seen(crescent1_supper_table) > 1: The supper table again. The butter swan is a butter stag tonight.|The supper room: a table the length of a barge, oysters on ice, a swan carved out of butter, and more silver than you've seen in your life, being used by people who don't notice it.}
text [12972a] = {seen(crescent1_supper_table) > 1: 又是夜宵桌。黄油天鹅今晚换成了黄油雄鹿。|夜宵厅：一张驳船那么长的桌子，冰上的牡蛎，一只黄油雕的天鹅，还有你这辈子见过最多的银器，被一群根本没注意到它们的人用着。}
# en: A long supper table under candelabra laid with silver, oysters and towers of ices, guests crowding it, a student slipping a silver spoon into a sleeve.
scene [a941c9] = 烛台下一张摆满银器的长夜宵桌，牡蛎和一座座冰淇淋塔，客人们围着，一个学生把一把银勺塞进袖子。
# en: Eat an ice and leave
opt.left.label [ce7f0d] = 吃个冰淇淋就走
# en: {seen(crescent1_supper_table) > 1: You take an oyster, and then your leave.|You eat an ice the size of your fist, for courage, and go home instead.}
opt.left.say.1 [e8118c] = {seen(crescent1_supper_table) > 1: 你吃了个牡蛎，然后告辞了。|你吃了个拳头那么大的冰淇淋壮胆，然后回家了。}
# en: Pocket a little silver
opt.right.label [a7aea9] = 顺点银器
# en: {seen(crescent1_supper_table) > 1: You pocket a silver ice-spoon and feel sick about it, and go on.|A silver spoon goes up your sleeve, and a salt-cellar into your pocket. A footman across the room sees, you're almost sure, and says nothing. You go on with your stomach in a knot.}
opt.right.say.1 [bc78e6] = {seen(crescent1_supper_table) > 1: 你把一把银冰淇淋勺塞进口袋，心里直犯恶心，继续往前。|一把银勺进了你的袖子，一只盐碟进了你的口袋。屋子那头一个男仆看见了，你几乎可以肯定，可他什么也没说。你揪着心继续往前。}

@event crescent1_conservatory
# en: The Conservatory
title [71541b] = 温室
# en: {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: The conservatory again, the orchids, the iron stair. The couple behind the palms are a different couple.|Off the ballroom there's a conservatory, {season == "winter": warm as summer|hot as a kitchen, every pane open}, palms and orchids and a fountain, and in the corner a little iron stair going up into the house. Nobody's here but a couple behind the palms, and they aren't looking.} For a moment the house is only a party.
text [afcd49] = {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: 又是温室，兰花，铁楼梯。棕榈后面那一对换了一对。|舞厅边上有间温室，{season == "winter": 暖得像夏天|热得像厨房，每块窗玻璃都开着}，棕榈、兰花和一个喷泉，角落里一道小铁楼梯通到宅子楼上。这里只有棕榈后面的一对，他们没在看。} 有那么一会儿，这宅子只是一场派对。
# en: A warm glass conservatory full of palms and orchids at night, lamplight from the ballroom through the glass, a small iron stair spiralling up into the house, a student among the plants.
scene [91bced] = 夜里一间满是棕榈和兰花的温暖玻璃温室，舞厅的灯光透过玻璃，一道小铁螺旋梯通进宅子，一个学生站在植物中间。
# en: Go back out through the ballroom
opt.left.label [c93412] = 从舞厅出去
# en: {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: You leave the orchids to the couple and go home.|You go back through the ballroom and out, {season == "winter": warm from the hothouse, into the cold|smelling of orchids, into the warm night}.}
opt.left.say.1 [b8c9f4] = {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: 你把兰花留给那一对，回家了。|你穿过舞厅出去，{season == "winter": 带着温室的暖意，走进寒冷里|身上一股兰花味，走进暖和的夜里}。}
# en: Take the iron stair
opt.right.label [e92b8c] = 走铁楼梯
# en: {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: Up the iron stair, quiet as you can on iron, and out behind the curtain.|You go up the little iron stair among the hanging ferns, and come out on the upper floor behind a curtain.}
opt.right.say.1 [c0aa24] = {seen(crescent1_conservatory) > 1: 上铁楼梯，在铁上尽可能地轻，从帘子后面出来。|你在垂挂的蕨叶间走上小铁楼梯，从楼上一道帘子后面出来。}

@event crescent2_back_stairs
# en: The Back Stairs
title [e263e7] = 后楼梯
# en: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: The back stairs, busier than ever. Somebody's left a full tray on the landing.|The back stairs, where the servants run: trays going up, trays coming down, a cook shouting from below. The study is at the top.} {flag(crescent_servants_hour): It's nearly eleven, and they're changing over.|}
text [ce6def] = {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: 后楼梯，比哪次都忙。有人把一满托盘落在了楼梯平台上。|后楼梯，仆人们跑上跑下的地方：托盘上去，托盘下来，厨娘在楼下喊。书房在楼梯顶上。} {flag(crescent_servants_hour): 快十一点了，他们在换班。|}
# en: A narrow servants' staircase in a grand house, maids and footmen hurrying up and down with trays, a student in evening clothes carrying a tray among them.
scene [66c8ac] = 大宅里一道窄窄的仆人楼梯，女仆男仆端着托盘上下忙碌，一个穿晚礼服的学生端着托盘混在其中。
# en: Go down and out by the mews
opt.left.label [3ad546] = 下楼从马厩巷出去
# en: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: You slip down the back stairs and out into the mews, and breathe.|You go down with the empty trays and out by the mews door.}
opt.left.say.1 [b90cca] = {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: 你溜下后楼梯，出了马厩巷，喘了口气。|你跟着空托盘下楼，从马厩巷的门出去了。}
# en: Carry a tray up
opt.right.label [3e87ce] = 端个托盘上去
# en: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: You go up with a tray of ices, and the housekeeper herself holds the door for you.|You pick up a tray of glasses and go up with the others, eyes down. Nobody looks at a tray.}
opt.right.say.1 [360a56] = {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: 你端着一盘冰淇淋上去，管家亲自为你扶着门。|你端起一托盘杯子，低着眼跟别人一起上楼。没人会看托盘一眼。}
# en: {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: You hold the tray like a guest, not a servant, and a footman sees it at once.|The housekeeper stops you on the stair. "I don't know you," she says, and takes the tray.}
opt.right.say.2 [430bec] = {seen(crescent2_back_stairs) > 1: 你端托盘的样子像客人不像仆人，一个男仆马上就看出来了。|管家在楼梯上拦住你。“我不认识你，”她说着把托盘接了过去。}

@event crescent2_lapdog
# en: The Lapdog
title [a313d5] = 哈巴狗
# en: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: The lapdog again, in the corridor, in its collar. It remembers you, and it's taking a breath.|In the middle of the upstairs corridor stands a small, fat dog in a jewelled collar, and it's taking a deep breath.}
text [274cba] = {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: 又是那只哈巴狗，在走廊里，戴着项圈。它记得你，正在吸气。|楼上走廊正中站着一只戴镶宝石项圈的胖小狗，正深深吸了一口气。}
# en: A small fat pug with a jewelled collar standing in the middle of a grand upstairs corridor, about to bark, a student crouching with a biscuit held out.
scene [4e239b] = 宏伟的楼上走廊正中站着一只戴镶宝石项圈的胖哈巴狗，正要叫，一个学生蹲着递出一块饼干。
# en: Back away before it barks
opt.left.label [daea4b] = 趁它没叫退回去
# en: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: You leave the dog the corridor. It seems to expect nothing less.|You back away, very slowly, and go down and out.}
opt.left.say.1 [80aaf9] = {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: 你把走廊让给狗。它好像本就这么认为。|你非常缓慢地退回去，下楼出去了。}
# en: Make friends, fast
opt.right.label [628f94] = 赶紧跟它交朋友
# en: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: You crouch and find the right ear, and it rolls over before you've finished.|You crouch, hold out a hand, and scratch exactly the right place behind its ear. It sighs and rolls over. You step over it.}
opt.right.say.1 [9b25e8] = {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: 你蹲下找到那只对的耳朵，你还没挠完它就翻过身来了。|你蹲下，伸出手，正好挠到它耳后那个地方。它叹口气翻了个身。你从它身上跨过去。}
# en: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: It goes for your ankle and holds on, yapping, and won't be shaken off.|It barks: a high, endless, carrying bark. Doors open all along the corridor.}
opt.right.say.2 [046ff7] = {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: 它扑上来咬住你的脚踝不放，汪汪直叫，怎么甩也甩不掉。|它叫了：尖利、没完没了、传得老远。走廊两边的门一扇扇打开。}
# en: Palm it a biscuit from the supper table
opt.up.label [f801b4] = 从夜宵桌顺块饼干给它
# en: {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: A sugared almond appears under its nose. It forgets the corridor, the house and you.|A biscuit walks out of your sleeve and into its mouth, and the dog forgets you exist.}
opt.up.say.1 [000188] = {seen(crescent2_lapdog) > 1: 一颗糖杏仁出现在它鼻子底下。它忘了走廊，忘了宅子，也忘了你。|一块饼干从你袖子里走出来，进了它嘴里，狗就忘了你的存在。}

@event crescent2_dressing_room
# en: The Dressing Room
title [97ffa4] = 梳妆室
# en: {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: The dressing room again, the jewel case open again. She changes her mind every week.|A dressing room, lamp left lit: a dressing table, a tall mirror, and an open jewel case, the lady of the house having changed her mind about her necklace at the last minute. A portrait of her watches from the wall.}
text [7a1779] = {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: 又是梳妆室，首饰匣又开着。她每周都会改主意。|一间梳妆室，灯还亮着：梳妆台，高高的镜子，一只打开的首饰匣，女主人在最后一刻改了戴哪条项链的主意。墙上她的画像看着。}
# en: A lady's dressing room in a grand house at night, a dressing table with an open jewel case before a tall mirror, a portrait on the wall, a student reaching for a necklace.
scene [6ff69a] = 夜里大宅中一位夫人的梳妆室，高镜前的梳妆台上一只打开的首饰匣，墙上一幅画像，一个学生伸手去拿项链。
# en: Leave the jewels and go
opt.left.label [a16aa2] = 别碰首饰，走
# en: {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: You leave her her necklaces and slip back down.|You close the jewel case, for some reason, and go.}
opt.left.say.1 [db101b] = {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: 你把项链留给她，溜回楼下。|不知怎么的，你合上了首饰匣，走了。}
# en: Take what she didn't wear
opt.right.label [9e2ff7] = 拿走她没戴的
# en: {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: You take a pair of earrings, and don't look in the mirror at all.|You take the necklace she didn't choose. The portrait's eyes follow you to the door, and your own face in the mirror isn't one you like much.}
opt.right.say.1 [cefdb5] = {seen(crescent2_dressing_room) > 1: 你拿了一对耳环，一眼也没看镜子。|你拿走了她没选的那条项链。画像的眼睛一直跟着你到门口，镜子里你自己的脸你也不太喜欢。}

@event crescent2_writing_desk
# en: The Writing Desk
title [ab43f5] = 写字台
# en: {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: {flag(jory_freed): The writing desk again. No new letters in the cramped hand: its writer is in the cells, and the shipowner's other correspondents are more careful.|The writing desk again. Another bundle has joined the first, in the same cramped hand.}|In a small panelled room off the landing there's a writing desk, unlocked, with a bundle of letters tied in red tape. The top one is in a cramped hand, and starts "The usual, by the side door, Thursday."} {flag(bonded_ledger): You've seen that hand before, in a ledger in a strongroom.|}
text [b730b8] = {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: {flag(jory_freed): 又是写字台。那个潦草的笔迹没有新信了：写信的人在牢里，船东别的通信人更小心。|又是写字台。第一捆旁边多了一捆，还是那个潦草的笔迹。}|楼梯平台边的一间嵌板小屋里有张写字台，没上锁，上面一捆用红带子扎着的信。最上面那封笔迹潦草，开头是“老规矩，走侧门，星期四。”} {flag(bonded_ledger): 这笔迹你见过，在一间保险库里的账本上。|}
# en: A shipowner's writing desk in a dark panelled room, a bundle of letters tied with tape, a student reading one by a shaded candle.
scene [fcabb3] = 黑暗的嵌板房间里船东的写字台，一捆用带子扎着的信，一个学生借着遮光的蜡烛读其中一封。
# en: Leave the letters and go
opt.left.label [4200cf] = 别碰信，走
# en: {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: You leave the desk to its secrets and slip away.|You put the letters back exactly as they were and go.}
opt.left.say.1 [6ac4e0] = {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: 你把写字台的秘密留给它，溜走了。|你把信原样放好，走了。}
# en: Read them through
opt.right.label [88e924] = 把信读完
# en: {flag(crescent_letters): {flag(jory_freed): You read what's left of the old bundle for anything you missed, and keep a letter that names a ship. Somebody would pay for it.|You read the new bundle. Same foreman, same side door, a bigger cargo. You keep one, and go on.}|It comes clear as you read: the warehouse foreman on the wharf, two sets of figures, and everything the side door let out came up the hill to this house. You keep the best letter. Somebody would pay for it.}
opt.right.say.1 [1444cb] = {flag(crescent_letters): {flag(jory_freed): 你把旧信剩下的部分又翻了一遍，看有没有漏的，留下一封提到一条船的。有人会为它出钱。|你读了新的一捆。同一个工头，同一扇侧门，货更大了。你留下一封，继续往前。}|读着读着就明白了：码头上的仓库工头，两套数字，侧门放出去的所有东西都上山进了这幢宅子。你留下最要紧的一封。有人会为它出钱。}
# en: {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: The candle gutters over a letter and catches it. The smell of burning paper goes straight down the stairs.|You read too long, and the door opens on a maid with a coal scuttle, who screams.}
opt.right.say.2 [a458c2] = {seen(crescent2_writing_desk) > 1: 蜡烛在一封信上晃了晃，把它点着了。烧纸的味道直冲下楼。|你读得太久了，门开了，一个提着煤斗的女仆尖叫起来。}

@event crescent2_balcony
# en: The Balcony Ledge
title [54d1fd] = 阳台外沿
# en: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: The ledge again, three storeys up. The gardens look darker than last time.|The landing ahead is full of guests' voices, but the next room's balcony is a few yards along the outside wall, and between the two runs a ledge the width of a hand, three storeys up over the Crescent.}
text [7cbafe] = {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: 又是那道外沿，三层楼高。花园看起来比上次更黑。|前面的楼梯平台上满是客人的说话声，但隔壁房间的阳台就在外墙几码远处，两个阳台之间有一道一掌宽的石沿，悬在新月街上方三层楼高。}
# en: A narrow stone ledge running along the outside of a grand town house at night, between two balconies, the lit Crescent and the dark gardens far below, a student edging along it.
scene [8c143b] = 夜里一幢宏伟排屋外墙上一道窄窄的石沿，连着两个阳台，下面是灯火通明的新月街和黑暗的花园，一个学生沿着它挪动。
# en: Stay inside and go back down
opt.left.label [b5feec] = 待在里面，下楼
# en: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: Not tonight. You go back down among the guests.|You look at the ledge, and at the drop, and go home by the stairs.}
opt.left.say.1 [55bd99] = {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: 今晚不了。你回到楼下的客人中间。|你看看石沿，又看看下面，从楼梯回家了。}
# en: Go along the ledge
opt.right.label [c22ebc] = 沿着石沿过去
# en: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: You cross without looking down once, until you're over the rail.|You go along the ledge with your back to the house and your heels over the Crescent, and climb over the next balcony's rail into a dark bedroom, shaking.}
opt.right.say.1 [390eba] = {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: 你一眼也没往下看就过去了，直到翻过栏杆。|你背贴着宅子、脚跟悬在新月街上方沿着石沿走，翻过隔壁阳台的栏杆进了一间黑暗的卧室，浑身发抖。}
# en: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: You knock a flowerpot off the ledge. It lands on a carriage roof in front of the whole Crescent.|Your foot goes, and you hang by a drainpipe until somebody in the street below points and shouts.}
opt.right.say.2 [e06cb5] = {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: 你把一盆花碰下了石沿。它当着整条新月街砸在一辆马车顶上。|你脚下一滑，吊在一根排水管上，直到街上有人指着你喊起来。}
# en: Step from shadow to shadow
opt.up.label [ea3d30] = 从一片阴影到另一片阴影
# en: {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: Shadow to shadow, three storeys up. Your stomach stays behind for a moment.|You step into the shadow of one balcony and out of the next one's, never touching the ledge at all.}
opt.up.say.1 [2e41a9] = {seen(crescent2_balcony) > 1: 三层楼高，一片阴影接一片阴影。你的胃在后面停了一下才跟上。|你踏进一个阳台的阴影，从另一个阳台的阴影里出来，根本没碰那道石沿。}

@event crescent_safe_card
# en: The Safe in the Study
title [0ba8ca] = 书房里的保险柜
# en: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: The study, the wardrobe of a safe, the brass dial.|The study, at last: ships in bottles, a globe, and in the corner a green iron safe the size of a wardrobe, with a brass dial. Below, the ball goes on. Somewhere in that safe the whole of Port Calder paid for something.} {flag(crescent_safe): You've had it open before.|}
text [63b427] = {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: 书房，衣柜一样的保险柜，黄铜转盘。|终于到了书房：瓶中船，一个地球仪，角落里一个绿色的铁保险柜，大得像衣柜，带着黄铜转盘。楼下舞会还在继续。那个保险柜里有整个考尔德港付过钱的什么东西。} {flag(crescent_safe): 你以前打开过它。|}
# en: A shipowner's dark study, a huge green iron safe the size of a wardrobe with a brass dial, a student kneeling with an ear pressed to it, ballroom music faint below.
scene [afc160] = 船东黑暗的书房里，一个大得像衣柜、带黄铜转盘的绿色铁保险柜，一个学生跪着把耳朵贴在上面，楼下隐约传来舞厅的音乐。
# en: Leave it and go
opt.left.label [204cde] = 别碰它，走
# en: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: You leave the dial where it is and go down the back stairs with what you have.|You look at the safe a long time, and decide it isn't tonight, and go.}
opt.left.say.1 [f71fa3] = {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: 你让转盘留在原处，带着手上的东西从后楼梯下去了。|你盯着保险柜看了很久，认定不是今晚，走了。}
# en: Listen to the dial
opt.right.label [a6f926] = 听转盘
# en: {flag(crescent_safe): The tumblers fall for you again. The safe has been refilled since; the shipowner has had a good season.|You turn the dial with your ear to the iron until the tumblers fall, one, two, three, four. The door swings out, heavy as a ship's. Inside: bearer bonds, a rope of pearls and a cash box. You take what you can carry.}
opt.right.say.1 [3c4003] = {flag(crescent_safe): 锁栓又为你落下了。保险柜之后又被装满了；船东这一季过得不错。|你耳朵贴着铁转动转盘，直到锁栓落下，一，二，三，四。柜门像船一样沉重地荡开。里面：不记名债券，一串珍珠，一个钱箱。你拿走带得动的。}
# en: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: You lose the count, start again, lose it again, and somebody tries the door handle.|The dial clicks, and clicks, and tells you nothing, and the study door opens.}
opt.right.say.2 [046a92] = {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: 你数乱了，重来，又乱了，有人在拧门把手。|转盘咔哒，咔哒，什么也没告诉你，书房的门开了。}
# en: See the number before you turn it
opt.up.label [e7ea2c] = 转之前先看到数字
# en: {flag(crescent_safe): You let Foresight run a breath ahead again, and the door swings out on a refilled safe.|You let Foresight run a few moments ahead and watch yourself open the safe, and then do what you watched. Bearer bonds, a rope of pearls, a cash box. You take what you can carry.}
opt.up.say.1 [7955c5] = {flag(crescent_safe): 你又让预知术往前跑一口气，柜门荡开，里面又装满了。|你让预知术往前跑几个瞬间，看着自己打开保险柜，然后照着看到的做。不记名债券，一串珍珠，一个钱箱。你拿走带得动的。}
# en: {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: What Foresight shows you is the study door opening, a moment before it does.|The moments ahead blur into music and footsteps, and the one you see clearest is a footman in the doorway. Then he's there.}
opt.up.say.2 [5de4c8] = {seen(crescent_safe_card) > 1: 预知术给你看的是书房门打开的样子，就在它打开前一瞬。|前面的瞬间模糊成音乐和脚步声，你看得最清楚的是门口一个男仆。然后他就在那儿了。}
